// =============================================================================
// Chora Content Creation — Question-batch acceptance events (Lane 1c)
// =============================================================================
//
// Emitted by chora-creation when an author ACCEPTS a batch question-
// generation job WITH the "Create test set" toggle ON (CHO-1703 / ADR-180).
// Carries the author-curated test-set structure (title / description /
// per-item points + display order) so chora-delivery can assemble ONE
// DRAFT test set without any cross-DB read (cross-DB queries FORBIDDEN —
// events are the only inter-domain mechanism).
//
// DISTINCT FROM the adjacent event families in this domain:
//
//   - chora.creation.ai_assist.*   — orchestration lifecycle of the LLM call
//                                    (started / completed / refused) — see
//                                    ai_assist.proto.
//   - chora.creation.question.*    — per-question authoring lifecycle
//                                    (authored / generated / evaluated).
//   - chora.creation.question_batch.* — this file — the BATCH-ACCEPT business
//                                    fact: N atoms persisted + the author's
//                                    curated test-set intent.
//
// Why the topic lives in the `creation` domain: the emitting aggregate is
// the question_generation_jobs row in chora_creation. The test set the
// subscriber creates is a chora_delivery aggregate, discovered by the FE via
// `GET /api/v1/test-sets?source_job_id={job_id}` (idempotent on
// test_sets.source_job_id — duplicate event delivery creates NO second set).
//
// Exactly-once intent: chora-creation publishes AT MOST ONE accepted.v1 per
// job_id (job-status guard, transactional outbox, BINARY encoding on the
// publish bridge — see the in_app.created dead-letter lesson). Subscribers
// MUST still treat job_id as the idempotency key (Pub/Sub is at-least-once).
//
// Per ADR-141: envelope.chora_imda_dimension SHOULD = "accountability" (D1).
//
// Aggregate root : question_generation_jobs (chora_creation database)
// Owning domain  : Content Creation (chora_creation)
// Owning team    : Team 1 (Content)
// Topic          : chora.creation.question_batch.accepted.v1 (+ .dlq)
// Surface (admin): A+ Creator mode (batch authoring review step)
//
// Subscribers:
//   - chora-delivery      — assembles ONE DRAFT test set (title/desc/items/
//                           points/order; source_job_id recorded UNIQUE) and
//                           emits the existing chora.delivery.test_set.created.v1
//   - chora-observability — D1 accountability evidence
// =============================================================================

